                  <photoshop:LayerName>The Njord SAA (Submersible Amphibius Aircraft)   is a remote co</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>The Njord SAA (Submersible Amphibius Aircraft)   is a remote controlled aircraft that can transition from underwater travel to aerial flight, utilizing deployable wings which fold out from the body.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>CAD by Jake Scholey (15) &amp; Coding &amp; PCB by Hugo Compton (15)</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>CAD by Jake Scholey (15) &amp; Coding &amp; PCB by Hugo Compton (15)</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Carbon fiber shell</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Carbon fiber shell</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>1.5 Kg Thrust  per motor</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>1.5 Kg Thrust  per motor</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Fiber glass shell nose cone </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Fiber glass shell nose cone </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Tailerons</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Tailerons</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Deployable folding wings </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Deployable folding wings </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>The PCB for the Njord SAA  is a standard 4 layer PCB featuring </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>The PCB for the Njord SAA  is a standard 4 layer PCB featuring all elements needed for a flight computer like an IMU, barometer, ESP32, and many pin headers for devices like servos, motors, and other sensors.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>816 mm consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incid</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>816 mm consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Quis ipsum suspendisse ultrices gravida. Risus commodo viverra maecenas accumsan lacus vel facilisis. </photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
            </rdf:Bag>
